    "result_text": "The build passes with all tests green. The implementation is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `ownerSegment` field on the owner response. Two changes:\n\n**1. `src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the `ownerSegment` schema property (read-only string enum) on the Owner schema, with the four allowed values `PREMIUM_METRO`, `PREMIUM_REGIONAL`, `STANDARD_METRO`, `STANDARD_REGIONAL`. This generates `OwnerDto.OwnerSegmentEnum`.\n\n**2. `src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a `@Mapping(target = \"ownerSegment\", ...)` and the deriving method, following the existing pattern used for `locality`, `timezone`, `ageBand`, etc.:\n\n```java\nprotected OwnerDto.OwnerSegmentEnum ownerSegment(Owner owner) {\n    String tier = membershipLevel(owner) >= PREMIUM_MIN_LEVEL ? \"PREMIUM\" : \"STANDARD\";\n    String area = REGION_TIMEZONE.containsKey(locality(owner)) ? \"METRO\" : \"REGIONAL\";\n    return OwnerDto.OwnerSegmentEnum.fromValue(tier + \"_\" + area);\n}\n```\n\n- **TIER**: `PREMIUM` when `membershipLevel` \u2265 3 (reusing the existing capped-level computation), else `STANDARD`.\n- **AREA**: `METRO` when `locality` is a known region \u2014 I reused the existing `REGION_TIMEZONE` map, whose keys are exactly `NSW`, `VIC`, `QLD` \u2014 else `REGIONAL`.\n\n**Result:** `./mvnw -o test` \u2192 `Tests run: 2, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2192 `BUILD SUCCESS`. Both acceptance tests (`STANDARD_METRO` for a Sydney/NSW owner, `STANDARD_REGIONAL` for an unknown-city owner) pass, and the rest of the suite compiles and runs clean.",
